#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:5 44f5cc2bf4b146068c1948c3aaa74b1c
msgid "Throw Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:7 db3f27934e4f489496f31bfc40844556
msgid ""
"This slightly dangerous flight mode allows the pilot to throw the vehicle"
" into the air (or drop the vehicle) in order to start the motors. Once in"
" the air, this mode does not accept any input from the pilot.  This mode "
"requires GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:12 900e9caf726845f8829112be750a7b80
msgid "This flight mode is available for multirotors only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:16 4de03eec718046db9dbb0660ce31ba0f
msgid ""
"Use with caution!  It is dangerous to get close to an armed multicopter "
"as is required to throw the vehicle.  It is recommended to takeoff "
"normally instead of using throw mode whenever possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:22 ef039420211a43f28e4e4232f50ecd72
msgid "How To Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:24 adf039f400cb418c93042555676ab9c4
msgid "Disarm copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:25 ee9989d9622949819c45a042af320985
msgid "Switch to throw mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:26 f8dda4959c1d4e83bcc26ee2e49b69ee
msgid "Check GPS light is green"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:27 496681859d394dfdb85b6dc8e70dfd3a
msgid ""
"Arm copter and listen for ready tune (if vehicle has a buzzer).  The "
"motors will not spin by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:28 968550752fbe42ad9739b707b2560ec0
msgid ""
"Pick up the vehicle and throw it up and away from you (it must climb by "
"50cm/s and reach a total speed of 5m/s)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:29 b0978df33fcd4f989edd4a8997f437a7
msgid ""
"Once the vehicle has stopped, switch the flight mode to Loiter (or other "
"mode) to retake manual control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:31 8860a451368a46d68e8915c043c984e0
msgid ""
"The motors should start when the vehicle reaches the apex of it's "
"trajectory. After the motors start this flight mode will first try to "
"control it's attitude (return to level and stop rotating), then stop "
"descending and finally it will attempt to stop moving horizontally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:35 00fa0c1bc01a4eb291294b3a61aa21df
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:36 a08eef7d6b7b498d8aec5dafed33207e
msgid ""
":ref:`THROW_TYPE <THROW_TYPE>`: set to 0 if throwing the vehicle up, 1 if"
" dropping the vehicle.  If dropping, drop from a height of at least 10m."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:37 28773cb51b13497191839ff9e4edb2a5
msgid ""
":ref:`THROW_MOT_START <THROW_MOT_START>`: controls whether the motors "
"will spin slowly or not at all while waiting for the throw (0 = stopped, "
"1 = spinning slowly).  The default is 0 (will not spin after arming)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:38 7cd946cf45544092939736dc05d25f44
msgid ""
":ref:`THROW_NEXTMODE <THROW_NEXTMODE>`: the vehicle will switch into this"
" flight mode after stopping (Auto, Guided, RTL, Land and Brake are "
"support).  Set to \"Throw\" (the default) to simply remain in Throw mode "
"and wait for the pilot to switch modes manually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:39 b45135817987421493ced409558204f1
msgid ""
":ref:`THROW_ALT_MIN<THROW_ALT_MIN>` and "
":ref:`THROW_ALT_MAX<THROW_ALT_MAX>`: set the altitude limits for THROW "
"mode launch. Throw must happen above the minimum and below the maximum "
"altitude above home after arming. Useful for plane or balloon drop "
"launches, allowing arming on ground to establish home altitude, then "
"rising in secondary release vehicle and dropping to launch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:45 52817d830caa419f87b15fde4a137918
msgid "Log Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throw-mode.rst:46 bb13486c63214ab88cba4331a8da4144
msgid ""
"During the throw, THRO messages are written to the :ref:`dataflash log "
"<common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner>`.  These "
"can be useful in diagnosing problems in case the motors failed to start "
"as part of a throw.  The graph below shows a successful throw in which "
"the overall velocity climbs above 5m/s and the vertical velocity is over "
"0.5m/s."
msgstr ""

